52","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99539","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2024-12-03T09:03:30Z"},{"id":2510707451,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6Vplr7","state":"APPROVED","commit_id":"f8f5505b263dca2951007b2013a5c8ee647bab6b","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3903059?u=1b0467024f137e562b21748eb6bf12f97dfa5bf6&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/raulsntos","id":3903059,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDMwNTk=","login":"raulsntos","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos"},"body":"Sorry for the delay. As discussed in RC, I believe this PR to be safer than https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99798 and according to the author of the other PR it fixes their issue as well.\r\n\r\nThis PR changes the locking mechanism from `lock(obj)` to using a `ReaderWriterLockSlim` instance, reducing the chances of a deadlock. The other PR moves `NativeFuncs.godotsharp_internal_reload_registered_script(scriptPtr)` outside the lock, and while this also seems to avoid the deadlock it can cause regressions due to underlocking.  So this PR seems safer.\r\n\r\nI was unable to reproduce the linked issue, but the code looks good to me.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99539#pullrequestreview-2510707451","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99539","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2024-12-18T03:33:05Z"}]